  "full_text": "Support for Nevada Public Radio comes from Sands Cares' Las Vegas Sands Corporate Giving Program, representing long-term, sustained dedication to creating positive outcomes and building a bright future in the communities we serve around the world. Click on the graphic for more information. But it's unclear if the rulers of Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, and Bahrain will take part. BBC News. I'm Kim Chakaneta, welcoming you to The Conversation, a program where we discuss the lives of women in the world today. Each week we hear from two women from different parts of the world who have something in common. One of my favorite places at school was the library. I loved being in a quiet space crammed full of books I'd read and books I hoped to read. But it's been years since I visited one, and that's mainly because now I can look up pretty much anything in seconds by reaching for my phone. So where does that leave the library? Are they a thing of the past? Or are they even more relevant now in an age of misinformation?",
